  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building National and Local Capacity to Combat Trafficking in Person in the Lao People&#x2019;s Democratic Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will establish local partnerships with community civil society organizations, who are already involved in informal cross-border coordination for the return of victims of trafficking from China and Thailand to northern Lao PDR, including, Village Focus International (VFI) and Sengsavang who operate both short and long-term shelters and protection-oriented support and have a deep understanding of the trafficking in persons (TIP) context in Lao PDR, and can offer survivor led responses to addressing TIP issues. Additionally, IOM will also work with and strengthen the community level coordination and capacity of local non-profit associations: Life Skills Development Association (LSDA), Community Based Drugs Alcohol Abuse Control (CB-DAC),Alliance Anti Traffic (AAT) and Namjai Community Association, all operating in northern Lao PDR.</narrative>
  </description>
